1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,859
You can flip this
floating magnet

2
00:00:01,860 --> 00:00:03,979
upside down. It hovers
over a

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:05,619
superconductor that is
kept at low

4
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:06,320
temperatures.

5
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:09,039
Inside it, magnetic flux
tubes are

6
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:10,720
pinned in place and
cannot move.

7
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:13,319
That pinning holds the
superconductor in

8
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,780
place, so it can
levitate.

9
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:17,419
This is called flux
pinning. But

10
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:19,069
the pinning also keeps
the magnet

11
00:00:19,070 --> 00:00:20,379
in place if the whole
system

12
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:21,130
is inverted.

13
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:23,080
Send this to a curious
friend.
